#. The Activities menu: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "menu.title"
msgid "Activities"
msgstr "Activities"

#. The Devices list: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "devices.title"
msgid "Devices"
msgstr "Devices"

#. Opens the Devices list, from the Activities menu and an activity's pages: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.devices"
msgid "Devices"
msgstr "Devices"

#. Back to the Activities menu, from the Devices list: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.activities"
msgid "Activities"
msgstr "Activities"

#. Back to the running activity, from its Devices list: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.activity"
msgid "Activity"
msgstr "Activity"

#. Back a screen: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.back"
msgid "Back"
msgstr "Back"

#. Leaves Delay Fixing, the Remote Assistant's note or the tour: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.exit"
msgid "Exit"
msgstr "Exit"

#. Keeps the delay chosen: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.done"
msgid "Done"
msgstr "Done"

#. Opens an activity's favourite channels, first on its page: a button's label, beside one of the four keys at the screen's corners; about 50 pixels, two lines at most
msgctxt "activity.favourites"
msgid "Favorite Channels"
msgstr "Favorite Channels"

#. Back to an activity's buttons, first among its favourites: a button's label, beside one of the four keys at the screen's corners; about 50 pixels, two lines at most
msgctxt "favourites.commands"
msgid "Commands"
msgstr "Commands"

#. A favourite channel given no name; {number} counts them from 1: a button's label, beside one of the four keys at the screen's corners; about 50 pixels, two lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "favourites.unnamed"
msgid "Favorite {number}"
msgstr "Favorite {number}"

#. While an activity starts, at the top; {activity} is its name: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line; cut to fit
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "activity.starting"
msgid "Starting {activity}"
msgstr "Starting {activity}"

#. While All Off turns everything off, at the top: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line
msgctxt "off.turning-off"
msgid "Turning system off"
msgstr "Turning system off"

#. Below 'Starting' and 'Turning system off': a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line. Each line break is a line of the screen, as Logitech's remote breaks it; a line too wide is wrapped again between its words
msgctxt "notice.keep-pointed"
msgid "Please keep the\nremote pointed at\nyour system"
msgstr "Please keep the\nremote pointed at\nyour system"

#. Help, at the top, while it sends the activity's power and inputs again: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line. Each line break is a line of the screen, as Logitech's remote breaks it; a line too wide is wrapped again between its words
msgctxt "help.attempting"
msgid "Attempting to fix\nthe problem..."
msgstr "Attempting to fix\nthe problem..."

#. Help, at the bottom, below 'Attempting to fix': a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line. Each line break is a line of the screen, as Logitech's remote breaks it; a line too wide is wrapped again between its words
msgctxt "help.keep-pointed"
msgid "Please keep your\nremote pointed at the\nsystem"
msgstr "Please keep your\nremote pointed at the\nsystem"

#. Help, above No and Yes: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line; four lines at most
msgctxt "help.fixed"
msgid "Did that fix the problem?"
msgstr "Did that fix the problem?"

#. Help asks about each device an activity turns on; {device} is its name: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line; four lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "help.is-on"
msgid "Is the {device} on?"
msgstr "Is the {device} on?"

#. Help asks again after sending its power: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "help.now-on"
msgid "Now is the {device} on?"
msgstr "Now is the {device} on?"

#. All Off's Help asks about each device: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "help.is-off"
msgid "Is the {device} off?"
msgstr "Is the {device} off?"

#. All Off's Help asks again after turning it off: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "help.now-off"
msgid "Now is the {device} off?"
msgstr "Now is the {device} off?"

#. Help asks about each input; {device} and {input} are names: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line; four lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "help.input"
msgid "Is the {device} set to the {input} input?"
msgstr "Is the {device} set to the {input} input?"

#. Help asks again after sending the input: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "help.now-input"
msgid "Now is the {device} set to the {input} input?"
msgstr "Now is the {device} set to the {input} input?"

#. An answer, over the bottom left key: over one of the two bottom keys, in the answer font; about 40 pixels
msgctxt "answer.no"
msgid "No"
msgstr "No"

#. An answer, over the bottom right key: over one of the two bottom keys, in the answer font; about 40 pixels
msgctxt "answer.yes"
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Yes"

#. Closes a note, over the bottom right key: over one of the two bottom keys, in the answer font; about 40 pixels
msgctxt "answer.ok"
msgid "OK"
msgstr "OK"

#. Leaves Help: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.exit-help"
msgid "Exit Help"
msgstr "Exit Help"

#. The note after an activity starts: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "assistant.title"
msgid "Remote Assistant"
msgstr "Remote Assistant"

#. The Remote Assistant's note, below its title: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line; four lines at most
msgctxt "assistant.note"
msgid "If any devices are not setup correctly, press \"Help\" now."
msgstr "If any devices are not setup correctly, press \"Help\" now."

#. Over the bottom left key, turns the Remote Assistant off: over one of the two bottom keys, in the answer font; about 40 pixels. Each line break is a line of the screen, as Logitech's remote breaks it; a line too wide is wrapped again between its words
msgctxt "assistant.turn-off"
msgid "Turn off\nAssistant"
msgstr "Turn off\nAssistant"

#. Help held down, the screen it opens on: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "delays.title"
msgid "Delay Fixing"
msgstr "Delay Fixing"

#. Delay Fixing, above No and Yes: a message centred on the screen; about 120 pixels a line. Each line break is a line of the screen, as Logitech's remote breaks it; a line too wide is wrapped again between its words
msgctxt "delays.warning"
msgid "You are in an\nadvanced delay\nfixing mode. Do you\nwant to continue?"
msgstr "You are in an\nadvanced delay\nfixing mode. Do you\nwant to continue?"

#. Delay Fixing's list of devices: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "delays.select-title"
msgid "Select device"
msgstr "Select device"

#. A device's delay menu, puts its delays back as they were: a row of a menu, beside its two keys; about 120 pixels
msgctxt "delays.set-default"
msgid "Set to default"
msgstr "Set to default"

#. A device's delay menu: a row of a menu, beside its two keys; about 120 pixels
msgctxt "delays.change"
msgid "Change Delay"
msgstr "Change Delay"

#. Choosing which delay to change: a row of a menu, beside its two keys; about 120 pixels
msgctxt "delays.power-on"
msgid "Power On Delay"
msgstr "Power On Delay"

#. Choosing which delay to change: a row of a menu, beside its two keys; about 120 pixels
msgctxt "delays.inter-device"
msgid "Inter-device Delay"
msgstr "Inter-device Delay"

#. Changing a device's power-on delay: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "delays.power-on-title"
msgid "Power On delay"
msgstr "Power On delay"

#. Changing the delay before a device's next: a screen's title, top left; about 100 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "delays.inter-device-title"
msgid "Inter-device delay"
msgstr "Inter-device delay"

#. Changing a device's power-on delay, from the left; {device} is its name; about 120 pixels a line, three lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "delays.set-power-on"
msgid "Set the Power On delay for {device}."
msgstr "Set the Power On delay for {device}."

#. Changing the delay before a device's next, from the left; {device} is its name; about 120 pixels a line, three lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "delays.set-inter-device"
msgid "Set the Inter-device delay for {device}."
msgstr "Set the Inter-device delay for {device}."

#. The delay being changed, centred above - and +; {seconds} is a number such as 4.5; about 120 pixels in the answer font
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "delays.seconds"
msgid "( {seconds} sec )"
msgstr "( {seconds} sec )"

#. After 'Set to default', from the left; {device} is the device's name; about 120 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "delays.reset"
msgid "Delay settings for {device} are now set to default"
msgstr "Delay settings for {device} are now set to default"

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words; {model} is the remote's name, such as Harmony 650
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "tour.1"
msgid "Welcome to your {model} remote."
msgstr "Welcome to your {model} remote."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.1.prompt"
msgid "Press the right arrow to learn more."
msgstr "Press the right arrow to learn more."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.2"
msgid "Use the arrow buttons below the screen to move between pages."
msgstr "Use the arrow buttons below the screen to move between pages."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.2.prompt"
msgid "Press the right arrow now."
msgstr "Press the right arrow now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.3"
msgid "The activity buttons above give you simple one-touch control."
msgstr "The activity buttons above give you simple one-touch control."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.3.prompt"
msgid "Press the right arrow to continue."
msgstr "Press the right arrow to continue."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.4"
msgid "The Watch TV button turns on the devices you use for watching TV."
msgstr "The Watch TV button turns on the devices you use for watching TV."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.4.prompt"
msgid "Press Watch TV now."
msgstr "Press Watch TV now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.5"
msgid "Buttons beside the screen select commands you can't find elsewhere on the remote."
msgstr "Buttons beside the screen select commands you can't find elsewhere on the remote."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.5.prompt"
msgid "Try one now."
msgstr "Try one now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.6"
msgid "The center button below lets you select the item above it."
msgstr "The center button below lets you select the item above it."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.6.prompt"
msgid "Press the center button now."
msgstr "Press the center button now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.7"
msgid "Use the help button if your activity doesn't start properly."
msgstr "Use the help button if your activity doesn't start properly."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.7.prompt"
msgid "Press Help now."
msgstr "Press Help now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.8"
msgid "The More Activities button lists all your activities on the screen."
msgstr "The More Activities button lists all your activities on the screen."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.8.prompt"
msgid "Press More Activities now."
msgstr "Press More Activities now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.9"
msgid "The All Off button turns off all your devices."
msgstr "The All Off button turns off all your devices."

#. Below a tour page's words, what to press to go on; a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.9.prompt"
msgid "Press All Off now."
msgstr "Press All Off now."

#. A page of the welcome tour after a write, from the left; about 124 pixels a line, wrapped between its words
msgctxt "tour.10"
msgid "You can now enjoy your entertainment system with one-touch activity control."
msgstr "You can now enjoy your entertainment system with one-touch activity control."

#. The tour's page about the center button: the softkey's word, centred at the bottom of the screen; about 60 pixels; about 100 pixels here
msgctxt "tour.center-button"
msgid "Center Button"
msgstr "Center Button"

#. Closes a firmware notice, bottom right; about 40 pixels
msgctxt "system.ok"
